  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"In two-point perspective, how many vanishing points sit on the horizon line?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Two\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"One\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Three\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"None\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"Orthographic views (front, side and top) are useful references for modeling to scale.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">How does sketching a concept before modeling save time in 3D?</p>\n  <p>Sketches let you explore shapes, proportions and silhouettes quickly, solve design problems before committing to geometry, and produce reference views to model from.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
